# Build backends for the wheels CI and the release runner image build from
# source: the CLI (cli/pyproject.toml: hatchling) and the Python SDK
# (client/pyproject.toml: setuptools, wheel).
#
# `pip wheel ./cli` used to download the newest hatchling into an isolated
# build environment, unpinned and unhashed, in the job that publishes the
# images. The jobs now install requirements-build.txt with --require-hashes
# into a throwaway virtual environment and build with --no-build-isolation,
# so the build runs only these files. scripts/test_ci_security.py fails a
# `pip wheel` that does not.
#
# Regenerate (in scripts/, needs uv):
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 requirements-build.in -c requirements-sdk-test.txt -c ../e2e-runner/requirements-lock.txt -o requirements-build.txt
# The two -c files keep shared pins (packaging, pluggy) on the versions the
# SDK test job and the runner image already install.
hatchling
setuptools>=61
wheel
